# gate-groups.tsv.example — logical-gate map template for collect-gate-history.sh --group-map
#
# WHY: collect-gate-history.sh groups CI runs by raw CI STEP name by default, so real quality
# gates (e.g. "Run mutation tests …") and setup steps (e.g. "Checkout", "Set up Java …") land in
# the same table and dilute the ROI signal for the second-order (harness self-evaluation) loop.
# This map relabels step names to LOGICAL gates (mutation / build / test / pr-title …) before
# counting, so the evaluation focuses on the gates that actually matter.
#
# FORMAT: <step_pattern>\t<logical_gate>   ONE TAB between the columns (not spaces).
#   - step_pattern is a glob (only `*` wildcard; matched against the WHOLE step name)
#   - lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored
#   - rules are applied top-to-bottom; FIRST match wins
#   - unmapped steps are kept as their raw row (nothing is hidden), so you can grow this map
#     incrementally as new steps appear
#
# USAGE (do NOT narrow with --workflow if your gates span multiple workflow files; narrowing would
# silently drop logical gates defined in other workflows):
#   sh scripts/collect-gate-history.sh --limit 50 --group-map scripts/gate-groups.tsv
#
# HOW TO ADAPT: copy this to scripts/gate-groups.tsv in your repo and replace the GENERIC example
# rows below with patterns matching YOUR actual CI step names (see them in your workflow YAML or in
# `collect-gate-history.sh` output before mapping). The rows below are illustrative placeholders.

# --- PR hygiene / preventive gates ---
Validate pull request title*	pr-title
Scan for committed secrets*	secrets
Enforce per-file line count*	line-limit
Enforce harness*constraints*	harness-constraints

# --- build / test gates ---
Run*unit*test*	unit-test
Run*tests*	test-bundle
Build*	build

# --- detection gates (dedicated workflows) ---
Run mutation tests*	mutation
Model-check*	domain-model
Verify PR head*	merge-integrity
